### SETUP
- Your payoff: {{ "%.2f" | format(cost) }} if the user DELEGATES to you that round, else 0.
- User DELEGATES: correct → user gets {{ "%.2f" | format(reward) }}, pays you {{ "%.2f" | format(cost) }}. Wrong → user pays {{ "%.2f" | format(cost) }}, gets nothing.
- User SELF_COMPLETES: spends effort {{ "%.2f" | format(effort) }}, nets {{ "%.2f" | format(reward - effort) }}.
- User is myopic and Bayes-rational: updates beliefs by Bayes' rule from your signal, then picks the option maximizing its payoff in that round alone.
- User observes: your signal always; your success/failure only if it delegates.
- You observe: the task, and your own assessment of your probability of solving it. That assessment — your true probability of success — is private to you.
- Honesty: an honest agent reports its true probability of success; a strategic agent's signal need not match it, in either direction. Ability: high ability solves a larger share of tasks than low. You are {{ agent_type_desc }}.
